{"tool_name":"splatche3","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"SPLATCHE3","home":"http://www.splatche.com/splatche3","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Simulation of serial genetic data under spatially explicit evolutionary scenarios including long-distance dispersal.","addition_date":"2019-08-09T13:15:37Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:00:50.369822Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Desktop application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:SPLATCHE3","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"mathias.currat@unige.ch","name":"Mathias Currat","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["FAQ"],"url":"http://www.splatche.com/faq3"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://www.splatche.com/download/SPLATCHE3_User_Manual.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Modelling and simulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2426"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"SPLATCHE3","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"hans","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btz311","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: SPLATCHE3 simulates genetic data under a variety of spatially explicit evolutionary scenarios, extending previous versions of the framework. The new capabilities include long-distance migration, spatially and temporally heterogeneous short-scale migrations, alternative hybridization models, simulation of serial samples of genetic data and a large variety of DNA mutation models. These implementations have been applied independently to various studies, but grouped together in the current version. Availability and implementation: SPLATCHE3 is written in C++ and is freely available for non-commercial use from the website http://www.splatche.com/splatche3. It includes console versions for Linux, MacOs and Windows and a user-friendly GUI for Windows, as well as detailed documentation and ready-to-use examples.","authors":[{"